WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:19.476
Since I had already cleaned my room, we decided to test the Amazing Mess-Pusher in Molly's room.

2
00:00:19.477 --> 00:00:23.790
We used it to push everything on the floor under Molly's bed.

3
00:00:23.791 --> 00:00:28.288
"Hey," said Molly, looking around her empty floor.

4
00:00:28.289 --> 00:00:31.079
"It really works, Iggy!"

5
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:36.199
"Yeah, your room looks nice and neat," I said.

6
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:40.645
That night I went to bed feeling happy about my new invention.

7
00:00:40.646 --> 00:00:44.080
I could help kids everywhere with their messy rooms!

8
00:00:44.081 --> 00:00:52.073
Maybe soon I'd also think of a new idea to help Molly with her monster problem.

9
00:00:52.074 --> 00:00:57.175
The next day Mrs. Romano asked us to take out our story ideas.

10
00:00:57.176 --> 00:01:01.244
"Tomorrow you will start writing your books," she said.

11
00:01:01.245 --> 00:01:05.442
"Make sure you have a really good plot idea."

12
00:01:05.443 --> 00:01:10.244
"Uh-oh," said Molly, rummaging through her backpack.

13
00:01:10.245 --> 00:01:15.268
"I think I left our list of plot ideas in my room."

14
00:01:15.269 --> 00:01:20.134
When we got home from school, Molly and I looked for our list in her room.

15
00:01:20.135 --> 00:01:22.825
But we couldn't find it.

16
00:01:22.826 --> 00:01:30.156
"I bet it got pushed under my bed with the Amazing Mess-Pusher," said Molly.

17
00:01:30.157 --> 00:01:32.416
Molly peered under her bed.

18
00:01:32.417 --> 00:01:36.331
"Oh no!" she cried.

19
00:01:36.332 --> 00:01:39.167
"What's the matter?" I asked.

20
00:01:39.168 --> 00:01:43.159
"There's nothing under my bed," said Molly.

21
00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:46.611
"Everything is gone!"

22
00:01:46.612 --> 00:01:51.796
"I wonder what happened," I said.

23
00:01:51.797 --> 00:01:57.041
"Maybe Caswell knows," said Molly.

24
00:01:57.042 --> 00:02:05.737
We went out to the living room, where Caswell and Lucy were watching another episode of Monster Madness.

25
00:02:05.738 --> 00:02:10.158
"Caswell," Molly said, trying not to look at the TV.

26
00:02:10.159 --> 00:02:13.915
"Did you take anything out of my room?"

27
00:02:13.916 --> 00:02:21.752
"Grr!" said Caswell, growling like the monster.

28
00:02:21.753 --> 00:02:25.540
But he shook his head to tell Molly "no."

29
00:02:25.541 --> 00:02:30.534
Lucy didn't know anything about the stuff under the bed either.

30
00:02:30.535 --> 00:02:35.495
We were still looking for our list when Molly's mom came home.

31
00:02:35.496 --> 00:02:42.152
"Mom, do you know what happened to the stuff under my bed?" asked Molly.

32
00:02:42.153 --> 00:02:46.444
"I cleaned the apartment this morning," said Mrs. O'Donnell.

33
00:02:46.445 --> 00:02:49.826
"I cleaned under your bed too."

34
00:02:49.827 --> 00:02:53.331
"Did you see a list?" Molly asked.

35
00:02:53.332 --> 00:02:55.746
Mrs. O'Donnell shrugged.

36
00:02:55.747 --> 00:02:59.890
"There was lots of stuff under your bed, Molly, including crumpled paper.

37
00:02:59.891 --> 00:03:02.704
I just threw everything out."

38
00:03:02.705 --> 00:03:06.622
So that was the end of our list of plot ideas.

39
00:03:06.623 --> 00:03:12.288
And that was the reason Molly and I had to start all over again.

40
00:03:12.289 --> 00:03:19.315
At school the next morning, everyone was complaining about how hard it was to think of plots for their stories.

41
00:03:19.316 --> 00:03:23.954
Mrs. Romano said Gina and Jake's story was missing a middle.

42
00:03:23.955 --> 00:03:29.981
"You only have a beginning and an end," Mrs. Romano explained.

43
00:03:29.982 --> 00:03:33.925
"How do you write a middle?" asked Jake.

44
00:03:33.926 --> 00:03:39.495
"Something has to go wrong," explained Mrs. Romano.

45
00:03:39.496 --> 00:03:43.290
"That gives a story suspense."

46
00:03:43.291 --> 00:03:48.242
Something definitely went wrong when I got home from school that day.

47
00:03:48.243 --> 00:03:53.278
There, in the middle of my room, was a garbage bag.

48
00:03:53.279 --> 00:03:56.049
On it was a note from Tate.

49
00:03:56.050 --> 00:04:00.527
"Dear Piggy, I found more junk in my closet.

50
00:04:00.528 --> 00:04:04.111
You can use your Amazing Mess-Pusher to clean it up.

51
00:04:04.112 --> 00:04:08.484
Just don't push any stuff under my bed! Tate."

52
00:04:08.485 --> 00:04:11.980
I'm normally a calm person.

53
00:04:11.981 --> 00:04:14.858
But at that moment I blew up.

54
00:04:14.859 --> 00:04:16.592
Everything was going wrong!

55
00:04:16.593 --> 00:04:20.796
My Amazing Mess-Pusher had caused our plot list to get thrown out.

56
00:04:20.797 --> 00:04:23.655
Molly was still not sleeping.

57
00:04:23.656 --> 00:04:28.065
And Tate was being mean and driving me crazy!

58
00:04:28.066 --> 00:04:33.814
"I can't stand it!" I yelled. "Nothing is going right!"

59
00:04:33.815 --> 00:04:41.241
Then I kicked the garbage bag as hard as I could.
